@Pratyoosh07 
> The exetension is nowdays in effiecient in blocking ads

Hi. Could you please describe how do you open Youtube - in the running browser, or open right after browser start? Do you see ads after refreshing the page?

Yes, it's by design, so it's best to contact with the site owner. There are some options with user rules:
- hide it when it's closed
```adblock
raw1001.net,mangakoma01.net#$#.dropMenu ~ ul.genresList { display: none !important; }
raw1001.net,mangakoma01.net#$#.dropMenu:checked ~ ul.genresList { display: block !important; }
```
- change the menu to scroll the links there (you can leave or remove a second rule).
```adblock
raw1001.net,mangakoma01.net#$#.dropMenu ~ ul.genresList { max-height: calc(100vh - 80px) !important; overflow-y: auto !important; scrollbar-width: thin !important; }
raw1001.net,mangakoma01.net#$#.dropMenu ~ ul.genresList a { padding: 5px 10px !important; font-size: 13px !important; line-height: 1.3 !important; }
```

